{
	"name": "Bulletcatch",
	"type": "maneuver",
	"img": "icons/weapons/guns/gun-pistol-flintlock.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Taking a hit dramatically, you wheel and turn before collapsing to the dust, just long enough to get your enemy close. When you are hit by a ranged attack, you can use your reaction to negate the damage. Whether you catch the bullet in your teeth or it hits a flask of whiskey in your pocket, or simply narrowly missed is up to you. Make a Performance check. If you beat the passive Insight of a creature who witnesses the fall, they believe you were killed, or desperately wounded, by the attack. Your first attack on your next turn against a creature you beat with your Performance check is made with advantage and is a critical hit if it hits the target.</p>",
